{"id": "85980", "name": "נגזרת של e^(xⁿ+a·e^x) – כלל השרשרת (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>Find the following derivative:</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\( \\displaystyle \\frac{d}{d{{CT:0}}}({{CT:1}}) = \\) [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Applying the chain rule</b><br>The simplest way to solve this problem is using the chain rule by defining \\(f({{CT:0}})={{CT:1}}\\) and \\(g({{CT:0}})={{CT:2}}\\) so that \\(f({{CT:0}})=e^{g({{CT:0}})}\\).<div style=\"background:#FFF8E6;border:1px solid #E8D29A;border-radius:10px;padding:10px 14px;margin:12px 0\">The chain rule: \\( \\frac{d}{dx}f(g(x))=f'(g(x))\\,g'(x) \\)</div>So,<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\begin{array}{rcl}\\displaystyle \\frac{d}{d{{CT:3}}}[{{CT:1}}] &\\displaystyle =&\\displaystyle \\frac{df}{dg}\\cdot \\frac{dg}{dx} \\\\ &\\displaystyle =&\\displaystyle \\frac{d}{dg}(e^g)\\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}({{CT:2}}) \\\\ &\\displaystyle =&\\displaystyle e^g\\cdot ({{CT:4}}) \\\\ &\\displaystyle =&\\displaystyle {{CT:5}} \\end{array} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<span class='correct'>Correct answer, well done.</span>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<span class='partially'>Your answer is partially correct.</span>", "prtincorrect": "<span class='incorrect'>Incorrect answer.</span>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "Diff", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "diff(p,v)", "testoptions": "v", "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "Result-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "diff(p,v)/diff(pp,v)", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-1-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">You need to use the chain rule (\\(\\frac{d}{dx}f(g(x))=f'(g(x))\\,g'(x)\\)) as {{CT:6}} is a function of {{CT:7}}.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-1-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["p", "pp", "rdm", "v"], "nvariants": 4}